781,0.0]]]}],"hatch":[[[0.0,0.0],[0.0781,0.0],[0.0781,1.0],[0.0,1.0],[0.0,0.0]]],"settings":"$r_0 \\approx 1.475$, $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\phi = 0$","input":"Kodama's kink at $f = 1.25$, in units where $c = \\mu = 1$, solved from this spacetime's own $G^t{}_t$ and $G^\\theta{}_\\theta$ and the field's wave equation: a throat of areal radius $r_0 = 1.475/\\mu$, a mass $M$ on either side with $GM/c^2 = 0.390/\\mu$, and clocks at the throat running at $e^{h} = 0.703$ of the rate far away.","caption":["The plane of $t$ and $r$ ($\\theta = \\pi/2$, $\\phi = 0$) on one side of the throat, the same on the other, through Kodama's kink at $f = 1.25$. The functions are those of the proper radial chart at the same sphere, $\\eta = h$ and $e^{-\\alpha} = \\partial_R r$, and the rays obey $c\\,dt = \\pm e^{\\alpha - \\eta}\\,dr$.","The cones close toward the throat $r = r_0$ because $g_{rr} = e^{2\\alpha}$ diverges there, while $g_{tt} = -e^{2\\eta}$ stays at $-0.494$, so the throat is the edge of this chart with no horizon on it. A ray moving in from $r = 3/\\mu$ reaches the throat after $3.0/\\mu c$ and goes on into the other side."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains","einstein_tensor"],"version":"b97af81b80f8c4e8"},"slices":[{"view":"wormhole","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0$","version":"7baaefd13f7c0c60","lines":[[[0.0791,0.5],[0.8874,0.5]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.8874,0.5],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}]}}
